- [ ] `[DOC_REPRO]` `test_full_replication.py`: Single master script executes end-to-end pipeline and reproduces all figures and metrics.
- [ ] `[DOC_REPRO]` `failed_hypotheses_registry.json`: All rejected hypotheses, degraded regimes, and ablation findings fully cataloged.

---

## 4. Phase 0.1 Change Log & Audit Summary

- **Introduced 6-Part Criteria Taxonomy:** Formally separated analytical invariants (`MATH_INVARIANT`), numerical tolerances (`NUM_TOLERANCE`), and statistical algorithm tests (`STAT_VALIDATION`) from empirical research hypotheses (`EMP_HYPOTHESIS`).
- **Eliminated Artificial Pass/Fail Gates on Research Outcomes:** Removed requirements forcing trading strategies to be profitable, neural networks to beat baselines, or unconditional EVT models to pass independence tests during market crises. These are now explicitly classified as empirical deliverables where negative results are documented.
- **Fixed Stochastic Confidence Interval Flakiness:** Replaced single-run 99% CI test (which had a 1% inherent random failure rate) with deterministic seed regression tests and multi-trial binomial coverage tests.
- **Audited Itô Discrepancy & SDE Convergence:** Standardized Itô verification to ensemble $L^2$ error ($\sqrt{T \Delta t / 2}$) and explicitly documented regularity conditions for Euler and Milstein solvers.
- **Clarified Reproducibility Across Platforms:** Explicitly distinguished local bitwise reproducibility (same machine, library, and seed) from cross-platform numerical consistency (`np.allclose(atol=1e-6)`).
